The author writes:

…

[[Original strip: 1990-11-18.]]

I want you to create fictional social media messages for a setting in a work of fiction, providing posts, comments and usernames of various posters. Here is the post:
[Photo of Lydia Whittingham, lying sideways in her hospital bed, encased in her huge orthopedic fiberglass cast. She is wearing an extravagant and ostentatious 1910s style hat and oversized polka dot bow-tie. Her expression is simultaneously pensive and playful.]
@lwhittinghamjr (Lydia Whittingham): Here is entirety of my formal outfit at the moment. Can’t fit anything else over the cast.
And here is the comment section:
@mitannigmbhunofficial (Otto Loosli): Hope you are getting better. Sorry for not visiting earlier. Workload is overwhelming.
@lwhittinghamjr: Don’t worry @mitannigmbhunofficial, I’ll keep you informed so you don’t miss anything. @margritausfrankfurt is making you do errands again, right?
@hertigcaroline (Caroline Hertig): This hat is going to be famous. Remember @mireilleyeye using it in her music video? Wishing fastest recovery.
@lwhittinghamjr: Thanks, Carol! If I had my split dress back than she would have used it too!
@hommedeverite (Marcel Messier): Looking very particular, Lydia! @mitannigmbhunofficial, if you are reading this, I am going to use you house, OK?
@lwhittinghamjr: Cool compliment, Marcel. You forgot to wish speedy recovery, did you like my current looks so much?
@hertigeuropeouest (Albert Hertig): Wish you to get back on your feet fast, Mademoiselle Whittingham. You are looking charming as always.
@lwhittinghamjr: Thank you for your support, Mr. Hertig! You are making me blush like a girl!
@rezafazekas (Reza Fazekas): Lydia, I know what are you going through. Makes your fashion taste so much more impressive. Keep it up! If that’s no trouble of course.
@lwhittinghamjr: No trouble, @rezafazekas! Your words make my day!
@oneontopofanother (Wittekind Rechter): Can you keep these accessories until my shift, please? Would love to see them.
@lwhittinghamjr: Anything for you, Mr. Rechter!
@prophetessemagus (Salvatrice Messier): What a divine hat! Reminds me of my youth! You are so brave, Lydia!
@lwhittinghamjr: Thanks, Madame Messier! But was this style really popular in YOUR time?
@mcaravetta (Mercedes Caravetta): Looking fabulous, as always! Love the bowtie! Also, isn't it crazy that @hertigeuropeouest and @hommedeverite are in the same discussion and not fighting each other?
@lwhittinghamjr: Haha, indeed! Everyone is too charmed by the ravishing damsel in distress, if I may so boast.
@margritausfrankfurt (Margrit Loosli): Smashing! Wonder if its uncomfortable keeping such a pose.
@lwhittinghamjr: Thanks! Only slightly uncomfortable.
@mireilleyeye (Mireille Hertig): Groovy "outfit", baby! Wearing a hat and nothing else!
@lwhittinghamjr: I have my reasons! Thanks!
@glorialamhauge (Gloria Lamhauge): Wonderful inspiration! Fit for a painting! I have an idea: a whole series of "outfits", all consisting of mere hats! How about that.
@lwhittinghamjr: Thanks, Gloria. Actually already though about that. Unfortunately I don't have any more cool hats with me. Unless you give me some...
Write long, quirky, interesting, offbeat, amusing, unusual and flirty continuation of this discussion.
